Data licences differ from the MIT licence above.  Every input dataset
shipped under ``data/`` retains the licence of its original publisher;
see ``data/README.md`` for per-dataset attributions, DOIs and licence
links.  In particular:

  * The 109 NW Shelf wells under ``data/wells/`` are released under the
    bundle terms of the pyBacktrack distribution (see
    ``data/wells/README.md``).
  * The regional Sandwell & Smith vertical-gravity-gradient cut
    (``data/grids/vgg_nwshelf.nc``) is a region-cropped derivative of
    the public Sandwell V31.1 release; credit Sandwell & Smith (Scripps).
  * The regional Braz et al. (2021) ``D10_gmcm9`` dynamic-topography
    slices under ``data/grids/dynamic_topography/`` are region-cropped
    derivatives of the model grids bundled with pyBacktrack; credit
    Braz, Flament and Müller (2021).
